$)
$(
This default file is used to define the translation of VPD PDMS classes to the equivalent EIWM classes.
Note that the translation mechanism external to this macro will continue to use the VDP class ID if
no equivalent is found defined in this macro


NOTES.
=====

  1. 'SITE' MUST always be the first class in the list, even if it maps to itself!
  2. !!EIWMExport.Classes is used to store the class list array.
  3. PDMS 'Site' is equivalent to EIWM 'System' class.
  4. The format must be..... PDMS Class+EIWM Class.... With NO spaces.
  5. The "Begin" line must not be removed... it identifies the lines to load

$)
$
--Begin
SITE+System
ZONE+Area
EQUI+Equipment
NOZZ+Nozzle
PIPE+PipeLine
BRAN+PipingSegment
VALV+Valve
INST+Instrument
SCTN+StructuralBeam
PANE+StructuralPanel
FRMW+StructuralFramework
STRU+Structure
HVAC+HVAC
ISOREG+WorkPack
SPLDRG+SpoolDrawing
SPOOL+Spool
FIELD+Weld
ASWL+Assembly
ASMBLY+Assembly
BLOCK+Block
HSTIFF+Hstiff
HPANBO+Hpanbo
HPANEL+Hpanel
HPLATE+Hplate
Otherwise+Unknown
